From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: add Gemini entry stage ledger

The prior post-reserved-memory Gemini ledger retained no record after a
confirmed boot cycle.  That leaves arm64 Image entry and the MMU transition
unestablished.

Add one default-off, experiment-only ledger with four independent records.
The first two are emitted from the primary entry path while the MMU and
data cache are proven off.  They use no call, stack, literal pool, or
boot-register clobber.  All four exact persistent-RAM headers are required
before writing.  The later checkpoints use early ioremap before FDT setup
and after the reserved-memory scan.  Every stage accepts an earlier slot
only when it is empty or byte-exact and writes only its own slot with
ordered full readback.

Skip normal ramoops registration on the Gemini only while this isolated
diagnostic is selected, leaving known-good Gemian as the recovery reader.
The patch does not access storage, regulators, clocks, I2C, CPU admission,
timers, watchdogs, or restart controls.  It uses a synthetic,
non-certifying author identity, carries no sign-off, and is not
submission-ready.
